=== SURVEY ===
Surveyed existing widget patterns:
- WidgetShell: accepts title, icon, loading, freshness props (updatedAt, isFetching, isStale, isError, onRefresh)
- WidgetDetailCard (shared): takes entries: DetailEntry[] with label, value, badge, mono fields; handles empty state, compact slicing
- MetricBar: animated progress bar with value/max/color/label/sublabel
- useWarrantyDetails(): returns VehicleInfoEnvelope<Record<string, unknown>> from /tesla/warranty
- VehicleInfoEnvelope shape: { data: T | null, fetched_at: string | null }
- registry.ts: 728 lines, ShieldCheck not yet imported, entry goes after maintenance-tracker
- Existing similar widgets: VehicleSpecsWidget (uses WidgetDetailCard), MaintenanceTrackerWidget (compact/standard split)

=== REASONING ===
- Hook returns Record<string, unknown> — need safe extractors (asString, asNumber) for untyped fields
- Compact (cols<=1): show days remaining as big number + Active/Expired badge (matches MaintenanceTracker pattern)
- Standard (cols>=2): MetricBar for time remaining (days used / total days), MetricBar for mileage (current / limit)
  plus WidgetDetailCard for expiry date, days remaining, mileage limit, coverage type badges
- Unit conversion: mileage fields assumed in miles from Tesla API → convertDistance + distanceUnit from useSettings
- Coverage types: iterate known keys (basic, battery_drive_unit, corrosion, emissions, body), only show those present
- All strings via useTranslation('dashboard'), null safety throughout

